# Copy to .env.local (gitignored, chmod 600) or export in your shell. Never commit real values.
# Scripts that need secrets run `node --env-file-if-exists=.env.local …`; shell-exported variables win over this file.

# ---- Neatlogs (Tailor runtime telemetry) -------------------------------------------------------
# Project key. Only needed for `neatlogs doctor --probe`, `npm run smoke:trace` and TAILOR_TELEMETRY=neatlogs.
NEATLOGS_API_KEY=
# Only the US runtime project is verified by this build; other endpoints refuse startup.
NEATLOGS_ENDPOINT=https://ingest.neatlogs.com
# Required before runtime ingestion. Startup reads the existing approved Doctor trace to verify key/project identity.
TAILOR_NEATLOGS_PROJECT_ID=18c4b4b6-0b1e-4d41-9405-7960fc2d0aa8
TAILOR_NEATLOGS_PROBE_TRACE_ID=
# Telemetry mode is a plain env var, not a secret: TAILOR_TELEMETRY=disabled | captured (default, in-memory, no network) | neatlogs.
# `neatlogs` exports Tailor turn traces to the project and needs NEATLOGS_API_KEY in the PROCESS environment (exit 2 otherwise).
# Exporting a live-model run is a separate approval from the spend cap. `npm run dev` does not load this file; `npm run dev:live` does.

# ---- Anthropic (live Tailor agent; approval-gated) ---------------------------------------------
# Server-side API key from the Anthropic Console project "tailor-neathack". Enter it here yourself.
# Read only by `npm run dev:live`; never printed, logged, exported through telemetry or sent anywhere but api.anthropic.com.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Numeric USD cap (0 < cap <= 50) for live calls: a fresh, explicit total approved by you before any paid call (earlier caps are not authorisation).
# The server refuses to start in live mode without it. Each guard/planner attempt reserves from its exact UTF-8 input bytes,
# a conservative token estimate, framing allowance and configured output ceiling; there is no fixed per-turn minimum.
# It settles from provider-reported usage and configured model rates. Unexpected overruns persist a degraded ledger
# that refuses later calls. Estimates can differ from final Anthropic billing, which is authoritative.
TAILOR_LIVE_CAP_USD=
# Optional spend-ledger path. Default: spend-ledger.json beside TAILOR_DATA_PATH (so a new data directory starts a new ledger).
# TAILOR_SPEND_LEDGER=
# Baseline model and effort (verified against current Anthropic docs; adaptive thinking is the model default).
# The model must have a configured rate entry (otherwise exit 2). Effort: low | medium | high; xhigh and max are refused at startup.
# Output ceilings per call: low 4000, medium 8000, high 12000 tokens.
TAILOR_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
TAILOR_EFFORT=medium
# Optional separate classification model, with configured rates. Defaults to TAILOR_MODEL.
# Blocking classification uses low effort, at most 1024 output tokens and a 10-second timeout; it is also a paid call.
# TAILOR_GUARD_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# ---- Local developer inspection (not secret, local only) ---------------------------------------
# Enables GET /api/dev/sessions, GET /api/dev/spend and GET /api/dev/telemetry with header x-tailor-dev-key.
TAILOR_DEV_KEY=
